## auth login
Usage: partiful auth login

Authenticate an account in an interactive terminal.

Flags:
  --json
  --plain
  --no-input
  --version
## auth status
Usage: partiful auth status

Show the current authentication state.

Flags:
  --json
  --plain
  --no-input
  --version
## auth logout
Usage: partiful auth logout [flags]

Remove locally stored credentials.

Flags:
  --dry-run
  --json
  --plain
  --no-input
  --version
## events list
Usage: partiful events list [flags]

List events for the authenticated account.

Flags:
  --when
  --limit
  --cursor
  --all
  --max-items
  --json
  --plain
  --no-input
  --version
## events get
Usage: partiful events get <event-id>

Get one event by its public event ID.

Flags:
  --json
  --plain
  --no-input
  --version
## events create
Usage: partiful events create [flags]

Create an event.

Flags:
  --title
  --start
  --timezone
  --end
  --description
  --location
  --visibility
  --guest-limit
  --link
  --poster-id
  --dry-run
  --json
  --plain
  --no-input
  --version
